- An 89-year-old male patient at Hong Kong Sanatorium & Hospital has been diagnosed with Legionnaires' disease, with the Centre for Health Protection launching a nosocomial infection investigation. Laboratory testing of respiratory samples on July 6 confirmed infection with Legionella pneumophila (serogroup non-type 1). The patient’s entire incubation period (June 26–July 4) occurred in the hospital, leading officials to classify it as a hospital-acquired case. The Centre collected 10 water samples and 6 environmental samples from the building's water tanks and the patient’s ward; results are pending. The hospital ward's showers have been halted, with plans to disinfect the water system and install bacterial filters. Medical surveillance is being extended to other patients on the same floor;
